course: dictionary
lesson: 14127
title: Words about generations and time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Millennial» is a good example. It can name a person, or it can describe something. Read the words around it first.
explain: «My mum is a millennial, born in 1985.» Here millennial is a noun, a word for a person. Your mum was born in the early 1980s to mid-1990s, so she belongs to this group. Millennials are also called Generation Y.
explain: «The town held millennial celebrations in the year 2000.» Here millennial is an adjective, a describing word. It is about a millennium, which is a thousand years, or about the year 2000. The words "the year 2000" are your clue.
explain: «Millennial habits, like sharing photos online, are common now.» Here millennial describes habits that belong to millennials. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Millennial has three meanings: a person, a thousand years, and something to do with millennials.
fact: As a noun, «millennial» means a person born roughly between the early 1980s and the mid-1990s.
fact: Millennials became adults around the year 2000.
fact: A millennium is a thousand years, so «millennial celebrations» can be celebrations of the year 2000.
fact: Generation Z was born about 1997 to 2012, and Generation Alpha from about 2010 on.
exercise: In «My mum is a millennial», what kind of word is millennial? | *A noun, because it names a person | An adjective, because it describes something | A place where people live | A verb, because it shows an action
exercise: «The millennial celebrations lit up the town.» What does millennial mean here? | A person born in the 1990s | Very tired after a long day | A kind of phone | *To do with a thousand years or the year 2000
exercise: «Millennial habits, like sharing photos online, are fun to talk about.» Find and copy the word that describes the habits. | *millennial | talk | sharing | photos
test: Who is a millennial? | A grown-up who has never used a computer | Someone who is one thousand years old | *Someone born roughly between the early 1980s and the mid-1990s | Someone born in the year 2020
test: Which generation comes after millennials? | Baby boomers | The Victorians | *Generation Z | Generation Y
exam: In «The millennial generation grew up with the internet», what does millennial mean? | A thousand years | *To do with millennials, a generation | A kind of computer | Very old and out of date
